#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:446
msgid "Using Filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:449
msgid "Selecting appropriate Filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:451
msgid ""
"There are two file systems for utilizing the on-board flash on the ESP8266: "
"``SPIFFS`` and ``LittleFS``. They provide a compatible API but have "
"incompatible on-flash implementations, so it is important to choose one or "
"the other per project as attempting to mount a SPIFFS volume under LittleFS "
"may result in a format operation and definitely will not preserve any files, "
"and vice-versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:458
msgid ""
"SPIFFS is currently deprecated and may be removed in future releases of the "
"core. Please consider moving your code to LittleFS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:461
msgid ""
"The ``SPIFFS`` file system is used by default in order to keep legacy "
"project compatible. To choose ``LittleFS`` as the file system, it should be "
"explicitly specified using ``board_build.filesystem`` option in :ref:"
"`projectconf`, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/espressif8266_extra.rst:473
msgid ""
"More information about pros and cons of each file system can be found in "
"`the official documentation <https://arduino-esp8266.readthedocs.io/en/"
"latest/filesystem.html#filesystem>`_."
msgstr ""

